{
  "abstract": "Let b(n, l) be the number of parking functions of length n whose maximum displacement is exactly l, where the displacement of a car is the distance between the spot it takes and its preferred spot, and call the sequence b(n, 0), b(n, 1), ..., b(n, n-1) row n. The formalization proves two theorems in Lean 4 with Mathlib. The first, the staircase (Parking.staircase), says that for every n >= 2 there is a position p such that row n rises strictly up to b(n, p), satisfies b(n, p+1) <= b(n, p), and falls strictly from b(n, p+1) on, and such that row n+1 either has the same shape with the same p or rises strictly up to b(n+1, p+1) and falls strictly after it. So every row is strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing, except that the entry directly after the peak may be equal to the peak, and the peak stays or moves one position to the right when the length grows by one. The second (Parking.unimodal_via_staircase) is the corollary that for every n >= 1 row n is unimodal, which is Conjecture 6.5 of Celano, Elder, Hadaway, Harris, Martin, Priestley and Udell (arXiv:2507.07243). The numbers b(n, l) are defined directly from the parking process. The staircase is obtained by induction on n from two rules for the sign of the step b(n, k) - b(n, k-1): a positive step stays positive one row down in the same column, and a step that is not positive is followed by a negative step one row down and one column to the right. The rules are proved region by region: tables that Lean's kernel evaluates in exact integer arithmetic settle the small columns, and analytic estimates settle the large ones. The proof depends only on the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The unimodality had been proved before, by another route, in the formalization MegasKomnenos/parking-unimodality (PALOMAR-2026-11-25-000002), on whose library this proof is built. As far as a literature search found, the staircase is first presented by this formalization and the package from which it was made; that it is new is not established. The proof was found, written and formalized by AI sessions. A person has read the two Lean statements, with the definitions they use, against the statements in words; no person has refereed the mathematics.",
